{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The sense: how many evils passed over my people — <small>(they came)</small> — for at first he went down to Egypt to sojourn, and there he was oppressed." "<b>and Assyria without cause oppressed him.</b> Like \"for nothing,\" like \"he oppressed him gratuitously.\" The reference is to the exile of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:08.436238684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}